# EE 599 -- HW 1: optional settings for Part 9 only.
#
# Parts 1 through 8 need none of this. They run against a ScriptedModel, with
# no network, no key, and no cost.
#
# TO USE IT
#
#     cp .env.example .env
#     # fill in one of the sections below, then:
#     python check_llm.py
#
# .env is in .gitignore. Never commit it, and never paste a key into a source
# file, a notebook, a screenshot, or a homework submission. A key in a git
# history is a key you have to rotate.

# --- Option A: a model on your own machine (no key, no cost) ----------------
#
# Install LM Studio, load an instruct model, and start the local server from
# the Developer tab. Nothing here needs changing if you use the default port.
#
# LMSTUDIO_MODEL is optional: leave it blank and Part 9 uses whichever model is
# loaded. Set it if you have several and want to choose.

LMSTUDIO_BASE_URL=http://localhost:1234/v1
LMSTUDIO_MODEL=

# --- Option B: the OpenAI API (needs a key, costs a small amount) -----------
#
# Get a key from https://platform.openai.com/api-keys and paste it here.
# `python check_llm.py` then lists the models your account can actually use, so
# you can set OPENAI_MODEL to one of them rather than guessing.

OPENAI_API_KEY=
OPENAI_MODEL=gpt-4.1-mini
